[gd_resource type="AnimationLibrary" load_steps=5 format=3 uid="uid://cl3g7w0legs77"]

; legs.tres -- CHANGE-BRIEF.md revision 7.0.9.
;
; The two cut-out legs, and nothing else. `LegAnim` is the single authority
; for `Rig/LegFront` and `Rig/LegBack`; `AnimationPlayer` is the single
; authority for `Rig`, `Rig/Body`, `Rig/SwordArm`, `Rig/SwordArm/Blade` and
; `Hitbox`. **No node is written by both**, which is the rule as stated --
; one authority per NODE, not one player per scene.
;
; This exists because the author rejected a sliding swing. The legs were
; hidden during `swing` because the swing's body cells carried their own
; painted legs; those cells are cut legless now, so the rig can drive the
; legs under a swing the same way it drives them under a run. No
; AnimationTree: nothing blends, one clip plays per player.
;
;   legs_run      the gait cycle, LOOP_LINEAR, 0.500 s = two steps
;   legs_planted  a braced stance, held -- a swing that is not moving
;   legs_hidden   both legs off, for the cells that keep their own legs
;   RESET         the default pose, legs off

